.TH CODEXBAR-LINUX 1 "September 2026" "CodexBar Linux 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
codexbar-linux \- native X11 tray for AI coding usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B codexbar-linux
.RI [ --popup | --quit | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts a single-instance GTK3 tray frontend. Colored bars show remaining quota;
white shows consumed quota. Provider authentication is managed by the upstream
CodexBar CLI and provider tools. An X11 desktop with a tray host is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --popup
Open or close the usage popup.
.TP
.B --quit
Quit the running tray and popup.
.TP
.B --version
Print the frontend version.
.SH FILES
Legacy configuration at ~/.codexbar/config.json takes precedence when present.
New installations use $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/codexbar/config.json. GUI state and cache
use the codexbar-waybar subdirectory for compatibility.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
CODEXBAR_CONFIG overrides the provider configuration path.
CODEXBAR_BIN overrides the bundled provider CLI executable.
.SH AUTHORS
Linux adaptation by Aiden Lyu. Based on steipete/CodexBar and
Marouan-chak/codexbar-waybar; their MIT licenses are retained.
